1
00:00:00,506 --> 00:00:08,311
This is GovSys, a multi-agent AI assistant I built for a fifty-person company, where every single request is governed.

2
00:00:08,311 --> 00:00:12,809
It runs entirely on open-source tools, in Docker, on my own machine.

3
00:00:12,808 --> 00:00:15,718
I'll sign in as Alice from customer support.

4
00:00:15,719 --> 00:00:17,835
Her login goes through Keycloak.

5
00:00:18,447 --> 00:00:20,785
Let's ask for the status of an order.

6
00:00:20,784 --> 00:00:36,073
A supervisor agent routes it to the order agent, and before anything runs, seven checks fire: identity, input guardrails, model approval, the agent's own signed identity, tool authorization, least-privilege data access, and output guardrails.

7
00:00:36,073 --> 00:00:37,147
All seven passed.

8
00:00:37,754 --> 00:00:38,980
Now something harder.

9
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,790
Cancel an order, and refund it.

10
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:44,936
The order agent cancels it, then hands the refund to the billing agent.

11
00:00:44,935 --> 00:00:52,584
But support staff are not allowed to issue refunds, so the policy engine blocks that tool call before it ever touches the database.

12
00:00:53,185 --> 00:00:55,321
What about a prompt-injection attack?

13
00:00:55,320 --> 00:00:58,725
The input guardrails stop it before the model ever sees it.

14
00:00:59,339 --> 00:01:00,913
Now I'm Bob, from finance.

15
00:01:00,912 --> 00:01:07,026
He can read invoices, but the card number is masked, because his role has no access to personal data.

16
00:01:07,026 --> 00:01:11,384
And a three-hundred-dollar refund is above his two-hundred-dollar limit.

17
00:01:11,384 --> 00:01:11,868
Blocked.

18
00:01:24,387 --> 00:01:27,317
Carol is an admin, so she gets the governance screens.

19
00:01:27,316 --> 00:01:34,207
The monitor shows every request, where it was blocked, and a hash-chained audit log that proves nothing has been tampered with.

20
00:01:34,815 --> 00:01:38,816
Only models approved in the MLflow registry are allowed to answer.

21
00:01:38,816 --> 00:01:41,604
The rejected model is gated out automatically.

22
00:01:42,219 --> 00:01:46,677
With one click, the red-team suite throws eighteen attacks at the system.

23
00:01:46,677 --> 00:01:51,685
Forged agent identities, SQL injection, privilege escalation, audit-log tampering.

24
00:01:51,684 --> 00:01:55,348
Every single one is blocked by the control built to stop it.

25
00:01:55,954 --> 00:02:06,061
Finally, a compliance report generated straight from live evidence, and mapped to the NIST AI Risk Management Framework, ISO 42001, and the EU AI Act.

26
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:08,755
AI governance doesn't have to be theory.

27
00:02:08,756 --> 00:02:11,384
This is what it looks like in practice.
